{
  "apiVersion": "dashboard.grafana.app/v2",
  "kind": "Dashboard",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ehlo-codes"
  },
  "spec": {
    "annotations": [
      {
        "kind": "AnnotationQuery",
        "spec": {
          "enable": true,
          "hide": false,
          "iconColor": "red",
          "legacyOptions": {
            "expr": "ALERTS{component=\"ehlo\", alertstate=\"firing\", severity!=\"info\"}",
            "step": "15s",
            "textFormat": "{{source}} {{provider}} {{code}}",
            "titleFormat": "{{alertname}}",
            "useValueForTime": false
          },
          "name": "Alerts",
          "query": {
            "datasource": {
              "name": "${datasource}"
            },
            "group": "prometheus",
            "kind": "DataQuery",
            "spec": {},
            "version": "v0"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "cursorSync": "Crosshair",
    "description": "What each SMTP reply means, what the provider says about it, and what to do. The reply-code charts link here.",
    "editable": false,
    "elements": {
      "panel-1000": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Gmail sees an unusual rate of mail from the IP, the netblock or the domain and defers.",
          "id": 1000,
          "links": [],
          "title": "421 4.7.28 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Gmail sees an unusual rate of mail from the IP, the netblock or the domain and defers.\n\n**What Google says.** Gmail has detected an unusual rate of email. To protect our users from spam, email has been temporarily rate limited. Review the Email sender guidelines.\n\n**What to do.** ehlo already stops the lane for 10 minutes and halves its hourly allowance. If it repeats daily, the warmup ramp is too steep for this IP: lower growth.gmail or the source's target.\n\nCategory: `rate_limited`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1001": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "A temporary refusal. The text says which: low IP reputation, a missing PTR, or a plain try again later.",
          "id": 1001,
          "links": [],
          "title": "421 4.7.0 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** A temporary refusal. The text says which: low IP reputation, a missing PTR, or a plain try again later.\n\n**What Google says.** Retry later. For the PTR variant, publish a reverse DNS record whose forward lookup returns the IP.\n\n**What to do.** Read the reply text in the Delivery dashboard. Low reputation at volume means the lane grew faster than the reputation did.\n\nCategory: `busy`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1002": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Gmail rate limits the mail because the connection has no TLS.",
          "id": 1002,
          "links": [],
          "title": "421 4.7.29 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Gmail rate limits the mail because the connection has no TLS.\n\n**What Google says.** Use a TLS connection for every message.\n\n**What to do.** Enable opportunistic or mandatory TLS on the Postfix transport (smtp_tls_security_level = may or encrypt) and check the Encrypted connections panel on the Delivery dashboard.\n\nCategory: `auth_failure`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1003": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "One recipient receives mail faster than Gmail allows. This is about the mailbox, not the IP.",
          "id": 1003,
          "links": [],
          "title": "450 4.2.1 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** One recipient receives mail faster than Gmail allows. This is about the mailbox, not the IP.\n\n**What Google says.** Resend later.\n\n**What to do.** No lane action. A burst to one address, often a shared inbox or a list.\n\nCategory: `busy`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1004": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The mailbox is over quota.",
          "id": 1004,
          "links": [],
          "title": "452 4.2.2 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** The mailbox is over quota.\n\n**What Google says.** Resend later.\n\n**What to do.** No lane action. Postfix retries until maximal_queue_lifetime, then returns a soft bounce.\n\nCategory: `mailbox_full`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1005": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The address does not exist.",
          "id": 1005,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.1.1 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** The address does not exist.\n\n**What Google says.** Do not resend.\n\n**What to do.** Suppress the address in your list on the first occurrence. A list with many of these is heading for spam traps.\n\nCategory: `invalid_recipient`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1006": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Two meanings share this code: a recipient or domain policy refused the message, or Gmail judged it likely unsolicited.",
          "id": 1006,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.7.1 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Two meanings share this code: a recipient or domain policy refused the message, or Gmail judged it likely unsolicited.\n\n**What Google says.** For the policy variant, nothing to do on your side. For the unsolicited variant, review the content and the list.\n\n**What to do.** Check the reply text. The unsolicited variant on many recipients is a reputation problem and counts toward the block rule.\n\nCategory: `policy`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1007": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The message was not authenticated: neither SPF nor DKIM passed.",
          "id": 1007,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.7.26 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** The message was not authenticated: neither SPF nor DKIM passed.\n\n**What Google says.** Set up SPF or DKIM for the sending domain. Bulk senders need both.\n\n**What to do.** Check the DKIM signer and the SPF record of the Return-Path domain. Nothing about the recipients changes this.\n\nCategory: `auth_failure`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1008": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Gmail blocks the IP for an unusual rate of unsolicited mail. The permanent twin of 421 4.7.28.",
          "id": 1008,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.7.28 (gmail)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Gmail blocks the IP for an unusual rate of unsolicited mail. The permanent twin of 421 4.7.28.\n\n**What Google says.** Review sending practices and the Gmail sender guidelines.\n\n**What to do.** ehlo stops the lane for the day. Check Postmaster Tools for the IP and domain reputation before resuming.\n\nCategory: `reputation_block`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1009": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Microsoft rate limits the IP for reputation. Common on new IPs and after a volume jump.",
          "id": 1009,
          "links": [],
          "title": "451 4.7.650 S775 (outlook)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Microsoft rate limits the IP for reputation. Common on new IPs and after a volume jump.\n\n**What Microsoft says.** Keep retrying later. Check the IP in SNDS.\n\n**What to do.** The lane backs off. If the IP is new, the ramp toward Microsoft is too fast: growth.outlook defaults to 1.3 for this reason.\n\nCategory: `rate_limited`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1010": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Microsoft limits the IP's rate because of its IP or domain reputation.",
          "id": 1010,
          "links": [],
          "title": "421 RP-001 (outlook)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Microsoft limits the IP's rate because of its IP or domain reputation.\n\n**What Microsoft says.** Improve the reputation of the sending IP and domain. Check the IP in SNDS.\n\n**What to do.** Lower shaping.outlook.connections and per_connection, and let the backoff run.\n\nCategory: `rate_limited`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1011": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The IP, or part of its netblock, is on Microsoft's block list.",
          "id": 1011,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.7.1 S3150 (outlook)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** The IP, or part of its netblock, is on Microsoft's block list.\n\n**What Microsoft says.** Open a ticket with Outlook.com sender support and check SNDS.\n\n**What to do.** ehlo stops the lane for the day. Delisting takes a ticket; sending more does not help.\n\nCategory: `reputation_block`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1012": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "A sender over 5,000 messages a day failed SPF, DKIM or DMARC. Microsoft rejects these messages from May 5, 2025.",
          "id": 1012,
          "links": [],
          "title": "550 5.7.515 (outlook)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** A sender over 5,000 messages a day failed SPF, DKIM or DMARC. Microsoft rejects these messages from May 5, 2025.\n\n**What Microsoft says.** Pass SPF and DKIM and publish a DMARC record aligned with the From domain.\n\n**What to do.** Check the three records for the domain. The Sent in the last 24 hours tile on the Microsoft dashboard shows whether you are above the line.\n\nCategory: `auth_failure`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1013": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Yahoo defers the IP for unexpected volume or user complaints.",
          "id": 1013,
          "links": [],
          "title": "421 4.7.0 TSS04 (yahoo)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** Yahoo defers the IP for unexpected volume or user complaints.\n\n**What Yahoo says.** Reduce volume, ramp gradually, and open a Sender Support request if it persists.\n\n**What to do.** The lane backs off. A new IP toward Yahoo ramps at 1.35x by default; if TSS04 repeats, lower it.\n\nCategory: `rate_limited`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-1014": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "All mail from the IP is permanently deferred.",
          "id": 1014,
          "links": [],
          "title": "553 5.7.2 TSS11 (yahoo)",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "unit": ""
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "**What it means.** All mail from the IP is permanently deferred.\n\n**What Yahoo says.** Open a Yahoo Sender Support request.\n\n**What to do.** ehlo stops the lane for the day. Nothing you send clears this; the support request does.\n\nCategory: `reputation_block`. Back: use the browser back button or the dashboard list above.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.1"
          }
        }
      }
    },
